import Essay from '../layouts/Essay.astro';
---

<Essay
  docNo="02"
  title="How a product earns confidence"
  description="How validation, failure analysis, statistics, and revalidation turn NPI into a learning system."
>
  <div class="sub">
    <div class="sub__body">
      <p>
        At a third-party laboratory, I learned that evidence has to survive outside the team that
        created it. For regulated products, it can decide market access.
      </p>
      <p>
        In NPI, its deeper job is to turn what failed into what the product becomes next.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="sub">
    <div class="sub__head">
      <span class="sub__no">2.1</span>
      <h2>Validation challenges the claim</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="sub__body">
      <p>
        A test is useful when it can change the team's model of the product. A pass confirms a
        condition. A gap reveals an assumption.
      </p>
      <div class="pullquote">
        <p>
          Validation is not approval. It is a challenge to the design.
        </p>
      </div>
      <p>The point is not to finish the test. It is to sharpen the next decision.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sub">
    <div class="sub__head">
      <span class="sub__no">2.2</span>
      <h2>A failure is not yet an explanation</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="sub__body">
      <p>
        Root cause is the chain of conditions that made the failure possible. The failed component
        may be the endpoint, not the origin.
      </p>
      <p>
        Design, process, material, firmware and use environment can all belong to the same
        mechanism.
      </p>
      <p>
        A correction matters only when it breaks that chain. Revalidation proves whether it did.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sub">
    <div class="sub__head">
      <span class="sub__no">2.3</span>
      <h2>Confidence has to scale</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="sub__body">
      <p>One explained failure is knowledge. Statistics decides whether it travels.</p>
      <p>
        Gage R&amp;R separates measurement variation from product variation. LSL and USL define the
        margin. Cp and Cpk compare it with the 6σ process spread. Reliability tests whether time
        takes it away.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>
          Confidence is not a stack of passes. It is an explanation that survives scale.
        </strong>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Essay>
